sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant SK as Scorekeeper phone
  participant S as App server (authoritative)
  participant DB as Postgres
  participant TV as TV display
  TV->>S: connect /ws?court=west&role=tv (read-only, no login)
  S-->>TV: snapshot: no active game, idle Next up
  SK->>S: open /score/west?t=QR token (weekly, signed, court qr_version)
  Note over SK: token removed from the address bar
  SK->>S: auth {qr, device}
  S->>DB: check court qr_version (Regenerate/Revoke bumps it)
  S-->>SK: auth ok + 12 h device session (tied to that qr_version)
  Note over SK,S: Reconnects send the session, no PIN. A session from an older QR version is refused.<br/>PIN is the fallback. Bad QR codes and PINs lock only that device.
  S-->>SK: snapshot with the picker (today's games on West, not complete)
  SK->>S: load {gameId} after "Load 2nd Grade Bears vs Dolphins on West Court?"
  S->>DB: status scheduled to active (one active game per court, shared-floor rule)
  S-->>TV: snapshot: the game (TV switches by itself)
  SK->>S: cmd {id:"a1", SCORE home +2}
  S->>S: per-game queue, validate, reducer gives seq=42
  S->>DB: save history + append game_event (seq 42)
  S-->>SK: ack {id:"a1", seq:42}
  S-->>TV: snapshot seq=42 (home +2)
  Note over TV: Wi-Fi drops, clock freezes and dims
  SK->>S: retry cmd {id:"a2"} after a blip
  S-->>SK: ack {id:"a2", dup:true} (applied once)
  TV->>S: reconnect (backoff 0.5 s to 8 s)
  S-->>TV: full snapshot = exact current state
  SK->>S: cmd END_GAME after "Complete this game?"
  S->>DB: status complete, final score saved, game locked (no taps, no undo)
  S-->>TV: snapshot: idle Next up + last final score
